{"id": "EUVD-2026-93146", "enisaUuid": "64ad75b1-4161-30df-904a-d400321e42eb", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ni2c: atr: fix dangling adapter pointer on add failure\n\ni2c_atr_add_adapter() stores atr->adapter[chan_id] before\ni2c_add_adapter() so that the I2C bus notifier can match child clients\nduring registration. On failure the channel is freed but the slot was\nleft pointing at freed memory, which can lead to use-after-free in\ni2c_atr_del_adapter() / cleanup and also block reuse with -EEXIST.\n\nClear the slot on the i2c_add_adapter() error path before freeing chan.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:15:49", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2f5e42edbd232bf705dc5d3a91e06344237e63bb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1093835f6aef58a831298d93e0d93f244fa07b84", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eabf7a3d33cd9fad106d267d00cc842434de8e02", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a57d9592714506556e30188af72dd3bdb9f647b5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ad34235808b63a70ca4989b7a2852923193d06ef"], "aliases": ["GHSA-r8g8-p677-vvfc", "CVE-2026-98218"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0f7d9700-b9fe-322a-9891-fce1fa9c3a49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "360fd490-5989-397f-ab30-b4ed2b518013", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "429efba0-e39f-3c27-bbfb-bfeb470aee94", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a076a860acae77bbdcbd316541e5552e81fb1772 <a57d9592714506556e30188af72dd3bdb9f647b5"}, {"id": "4f92650f-670f-34ca-b17c-feae3b1fa6e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a076a860acae77bbdcbd316541e5552e81fb1772 <ad34235808b63a70ca4989b7a2852923193d06ef"}, {"id": "50b6b120-71c8-32b1-ad58-054fcdda3ebb", "product